{"parameters":{"model":"dxn:com.anthropic.model.claude-opus-5.default","stream":true,"tools":[{"name":"eval","description":"Runs code against the workspace and returns whatever that code printed. This is the only tool: every read, every write and every operation happens inside it.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"code":{"type":"string","description":"The program, in the dialect the system prompt describes. Print anything you need to see."}},"required":["code"],"additionalProperties":true}}]},"prompt":{"content":[{"options":{},"role":"system","content":"## Code mode\n\nYou have exactly one tool, `eval`, which runs the body of an async JavaScript function against\nthis workspace and returns whatever that code printed. Nothing else is visible to you: a value\nyou do not `print` never reaches you. Do not use `import` or `require` — the API below is\nin scope.\n\nPrefer one `eval` call that does the whole job — query, inspect, change, print — over a call\nper step. Print the specific values you need to reason about, not whole objects, and keep the\noutput small.\n\n### API\n\n- `print(...values)` — adds a line to this call's output. Strings go through verbatim,\n  everything else is printed as JSON.\n- `await query(typename, props?)` — objects of that typename, optionally narrowed by exact\n  property values, e.g. `await query('example.com/type/Task', { status: 'open' })`.\n- `await make(typename, props)` — a new object; it is not stored until you add it.\n- `await add(obj)` / `await remove(obj)` — store or delete an object.\n- `update(obj, (obj) => { obj.field = value; })` — the only way to change a stored object.\n- `await flush()` — waits for pending writes to land; call it before printing a final\n  confirmation.\n\n### Operations\n\nThe skills above describe their capabilities as tools; in code mode they are NOT tools. Each one\nis an async function on `ops`, taking one argument matching its parameter schema. A failed\noperation throws, so wrap a call you expect to fail in `try`/`catch`.\n\n- `await ops.com-example-operation-score(input)` — Scores a task title for urgency, returning a number between 0 and 10.\n  input: {\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"title\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The title to score\"}},\"required\":[\"title\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}\n\n## Skills Definitions\n\n<skill>\n  \n</skill>"},{"options":{},"role":"user","content":"Score every open task of type com.example.type.task and store each score on the task's priority field. Then tell me which task scored highest."},{"options":{},"role":"assistant","content":[{"options":{},"type":"text","text":"I'll start by finding the open tasks and inspecting their shape."},{"options":{},"type":"tool-call","id":"toolu_01LT5sFcV1oxUPLyBucTLcnJ","name":"eval","params":{"code":"const tasks = await query('com.example.type.task', { status: 'open' });\nprint('count:', tasks.length);\nif (tasks.length) print('keys:', Object.keys(tasks[0]).join(', '));\nfor (const t of tasks) print(JSON.stringify({ id: t.id, title: t.title, status: t.status, priority: t.priority }));"},"providerExecuted":false}]},{"options":{},"role":"tool","content":[{"options":{},"type":"tool-result","id":"toolu_01LT5sFcV1oxUPLyBucTLcnJ","name":"eval","isFailure":false,"result":{"output":"count: 2\nkeys: id, status, title\n{\"id\":\"01JGFJJZ00G0WKQSJGMAKCNTEX\",\"title\":\"Write the docs\",\"status\":\"open\"}\n{\"id\":\"01JGFJJZ00G0WKQSJGMAKCNTEY\",\"title\":\"Fix the build\",\"status\":\"open\"}"},"providerExecuted":false}]},{"options":{},"role":"assistant","content":[{"options":{},"type":"reasoning","text":"I'm seeing only 2 open tasks, so I'll double check the full task list to confirm \"open\" is the correct status filter before scoring them, since there's no existing priority field to compare against—I'll need to add that via an update.\n\n"},{"options":{},"type":"text","text":"Two open tasks. Let me check the full set (in case of other status spellings), then score and store."},{"options":{},"type":"tool-call","id":"toolu_019rvGuM7ESxQTmcbdZiaLFQ","name":"eval","params":{"code":"const all = await query('com.example.type.task');\nprint('total tasks:', all.length);\nconst statuses = {};\nfor (const t of all) statuses[t.status] = (statuses[t.status] || 0) + 1;\nprint('statuses:', JSON.stringify(statuses));\n\nconst open = all.filter(t => t.status === 'open');\nconst results = [];\nfor (const t of open) {\n  try {\n    const score = await ops['com-example-operation-score']({ title: t.title });\n    update(t, (o) => { o.priority = score; });\n    results.push({ title: t.title, score });\n  } catch (e) {\n    print('FAILED for', t.title, '->', String(e));\n  }\n}\nawait flush();\n\nconst verify = await query('com.example.type.task', { status: 'open' });\nfor (const t of verify) print('stored:', t.title, '=>', t.priority);\nresults.sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);\nprint('ranking:', JSON.stringify(results));"},"providerExecuted":false}]},{"options":{},"role":"tool","content":[{"options":{},"type":"tool-result","id":"toolu_019rvGuM7ESxQTmcbdZiaLFQ","name":"eval","isFailure":false,"result":{"output":"total tasks: 3\nstatuses: {\"open\":2,\"done\":1}\nstored: Write the docs => 14\nstored: Fix the build => 13\nranking: [{\"title\":\"Write the docs\",\"score\":14},{\"title\":\"Fix the build\",\"score\":13}]"},"providerExecuted":false}]},{"options":{},"role":"assistant","content":[{"options":{},"type":"reasoning","text":"Wait, scores of 14 and 13 exceed the documented 0-10 range for this operation—that's out of spec and worth flagging. I want to re-run the operation to check whether it's deterministic before concluding anything.\n\n"},{"options":{},"type":"text","text":"The scores came back out of spec, so let me probe the operation before trusting them."},{"options":{},"type":"tool-call","id":"toolu_01UGx7KswPE1MQsMbmVKvEvN","name":"eval","params":{"code":"for (const title of ['Write the docs', 'Fix the build', 'Write the docs']) {\n